{
  "$comment": "Built-in presets for the page-decoration dialogs (M53). Data, not code: PLAN.md §4.4. Each entry is `{ id, name, kind, spec }` and the spec is exactly what src/renderer/modules/M53-headers-bates-watermarks-links/model.ts validates, so a preset that gains a field an older build does not know simply loses that field rather than failing to load. Colours are `0xRRGGBB` numbers because they end up inside the PDF, not in the interface — theme tokens have no meaning on a printed page. Presets the reader saves live in settings, not here.",
